@startuml
!include _style.iuml
skinparam dpi 96
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowFontSize 15
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 15
skinparam LegendFontSize 14
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 400
skinparam sequenceMessageSpan true
skinparam sequence {
  MessageSpacing 2
  GroupBorderThickness 1
}
title Sequence view · UC-1 verifies bytes before adopting the source\nAs built at 76282d3
' Evidence: https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/api/uploads.py#L36
' Evidence: https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.py#L99
' Evidence: https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.py#L149
' Evidence: https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/storage.py#L62
' Evidence: https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/messaging.py#L31
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam LegendFontSize 16
skinparam maxMessageSize 320
participant "direct_intake\n«module»" as I $MEDIA
participant "storage: Storage" as S $MEDIA
participant "messaging\n«module»" as M $MEDIA
participant "s: AsyncSession" as DB $INFRA
[-> I : finalize(s,storage,owner,rid,request)
activate I
I -> DB : SQL: read owned, pending reservation\n(read transaction ends)
I -> S : verify_direct_upload(row)
activate S
S --> I : version_id: str
 deactivate S
group Media adoption transaction
 I -> DB : SQL: lock + recheck reservation;\npin version; add/flush Asset
 I -> M : enqueue_submit(s,asset,source(row))
 activate M
 M -> DB : SQL: stage MediaOutbox submit
 M --> I : message_id: UUID
 deactivate M
 I -> DB : COMMIT reservation + Asset + outbox
end
[<-- I : asset: Asset
 deactivate I
legend bottom
Caller: api.uploads.finalize_upload; it maps Asset to Accepted and HTTP 202.
Successful pending path shown. Replay returns the prior Asset; expiry/error prevents adoption.
Blue = Media; slate = SQL. Solid filled arrow = awaited call; dashed = reply. SQL labels summarize effects.
endlegend

@enduml
